y reach model context. If either is model-visible, use it for\n  the import notice instead of representing the notice as a user turn. See\n  [the Claude session-format spec](specs/claude-session-format.md).\n\n## Release\n\n- Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm, replace turnbridge's local `file:`\n  dependency with a semver range, and then publish turnbridge. The\n  `prepublishOnly` check deliberately blocks publishing before this is done.\n- Re-run the interactive, recall, invariant, large-history, function-call, and\n  picker probes against the release CLI versions. Adapter-drift automation\n  remains reporting-only; credentialed validation is a human-run release task.\n\n## Research backlog\n\nThese are non-blocking unknowns, not current release requirements:\n\n- Codex encrypted-reasoning blob lifetime and API-platform-organization auth.\n- Histories beyond roughly 300 turns and `custom_tool_call` fabrication.\n- Claude Code's picker sort key.\n- opencode's project-id derivation if a future release makes it relevant to\n  import placement.\n\nscripts/probe-picker.mjs:1:// Resolves the two picker unknowns the specs left inferred rather than tested:\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:130:minimal working schemas, unknowns): [docs/specs/claude-session-format.md](specs/claude-session-format.md),\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:217:  state for this target. Remaining opencode gaps: no headless model-recall\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:219:  unmeasured — see the spec's \"Unknowns\".\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:247:  Deliberately left unmeasured: histories beyond ~300 turns (both targets are\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:284:  Still open: blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves the same\nscripts/smoke-interactive.mjs:9: * cannot: the TUI render path users actually see. See docs/specs/* \"Unknowns\".\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:39:These are non-blocking unknowns, not current release requirements:\ndocs/specs/claude-session-format.md:356:## 7. Unknowns / risks\ndocs/specs/op